    {
      "id": "6f410d7c-f215-46e5-aa5a-c00e1e65a179",
      "name": "Why MCP Is Awesome: Giving AI Real Hands on Your Tools",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP Is Awesome: Giving AI Real Hands on Your Tools",
      "docTypeId": "0e8f35b8-9fc8-4f74-b54f-583c5df09b4a",
      "templateId": "14a8ccc2-777c-4284-8f51-efb44f75718c",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "The Model Context Protocol turns “the AI described what it would do” into “the AI actually did it” — through the same tools you already trust."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-09-29 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "f98c9535-1d13-4367-8567-c9994b6ac454",
              "mediaKey": "41fc0c4e-c4df-4eb9-8a6a-fb0525d5a746",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "f6703ddd-fbee-4b60-93e3-5c9d4eaec441",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "d3781178-8834-4789-9332-2870e075c1a9",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "52b1a28b-be82-4bf2-aba0-3a05215e91e3",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "91e73a5c-928c-4207-9fd0-7c2f593136e2",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "f6703ddd-fbee-4b60-93e3-5c9d4eaec441",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>One Protocol, Any Tool</h2><p>Before the Model Context Protocol (MCP), every AI integration was a bespoke bridge: a custom plugin for this API, a hand-rolled wrapper for that database, a one-off script for the third tool. Each connection had its own quirks, its own auth dance, its own failure modes. MCP replaces all of that with one simple idea: expose your tools, resources, and prompts through a single, well-defined protocol, and any capable AI client can use them — no custom glue code required.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "d3781178-8834-4789-9332-2870e075c1a9",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Why That's a Big Deal</h2><ul><li><strong>Write once, use everywhere.</strong> A server built for one assistant works with any MCP-compatible client.</li><li><strong>Real actions, not just suggestions.</strong> An agent can call <code>create-document</code> or <code>publish-document</code> directly, instead of describing what you should click.</li><li><strong>Local-first and auditable.</strong> Tools run where your data already lives, under credentials you control.</li></ul>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "a81ac966-1450-4676-a7e6-ee0d2b629e24",
                "key": "52b1a28b-be82-4bf2-aba0-3a05215e91e3",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "20a69fe4-ed28-4c36-b2b7-c9df32061c9c",
                        "mediaKey": "019fb4fc-f480-4ccb-8566-72fcdef29f51",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "A standard connector means every tool clicks into place instead of being forced. Photo by Edge2Edge Media on Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "91e73a5c-928c-4207-9fd0-7c2f593136e2",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>That's the whole pitch: less plumbing, more building. MCP turns “the model described an action” into “the model performed the action” — safely, locally, and through interfaces you already trust.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "f6703ddd-fbee-4b60-93e3-5c9d4eaec441",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "d3781178-8834-4789-9332-2870e075c1a9",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "52b1a28b-be82-4bf2-aba0-3a05215e91e3",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "91e73a5c-928c-4207-9fd0-7c2f593136e2",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/why-mcp-is-awesome-giving-ai-real-hands-on-your-tools/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": "blogPost"
    },
    {
      "id": "5a183a73-724a-424d-864c-7a10a6ba91c1",
      "name": "Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Infinite Integrations",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Infinite Integrations",
      "docTypeId": "0e8f35b8-9fc8-4f74-b54f-583c5df09b4a",
      "templateId": "14a8ccc2-777c-4284-8f51-efb44f75718c",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "Build a tool server once, and every MCP-aware assistant can use it — that network effect is what makes MCP genuinely exciting."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-03 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "b2394f3d-47ed-4ebe-9c8d-17af642fe649",
              "mediaKey": "5d7c5f28-d556-4cb5-932e-809fc0552683",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "979921c4-0f03-4201-88a7-46430b4d8244",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "02bc06e7-4037-48a9-a45c-d88feb3d4bf4",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "e8e2c9ff-b6b0-4c31-9611-653f81d92d07",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "c81a9271-d292-4a37-8201-e66f39280aaf",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "979921c4-0f03-4201-88a7-46430b4d8244",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>The Network Effect of a Shared Standard</h2><p>This very site is proof: a single Umbraco MCP server exposes document types, content, media, and templates as tools, and an AI agent used them to design, build, and populate an entire blog — folders, element types, a Block Grid, document types, templates, media, and these two posts — without a single bespoke integration being written for the task.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "02bc06e7-4037-48a9-a45c-d88feb3d4bf4",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<h2>Small Pieces, Composed</h2><p>Each MCP tool is tiny and well-scoped: <code>create-document-type</code>, <code>create-media</code>, <code>publish-document</code>. None of them know about each other, yet composed together they let an agent reason about a whole content model and carry it out end to end. That's the same lesson as good software architecture — small, composable pieces beat one giant bespoke system — applied to how AI touches real tools.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "a81ac966-1450-4676-a7e6-ee0d2b629e24",
                "key": "e8e2c9ff-b6b0-4c31-9611-653f81d92d07",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "6f0902b7-bb7d-4fb3-b274-9ce267a1fca9",
                        "mediaKey": "1911ea85-debb-4c84-a2f2-cd39a6cbc23e",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Composable building blocks: that's what MCP tools feel like to an agent. Photo by Shubham Dhage on Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "87607f02-d4ad-469c-b44c-fd587877caf4",
                "key": "c81a9271-d292-4a37-8201-e66f39280aaf",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The result isn't a one-off demo script tied to this project — it's a repeatable pattern. Any system that speaks MCP joins the same ecosystem, instantly usable by any assistant that speaks it back.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "979921c4-0f03-4201-88a7-46430b4d8244",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
